[32m+[m[32m# Lazarus Biotechnologies Documentation Standard[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Document ID:** LBT-DOC-001[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m**Status:** Active[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m**Project:** Lazarus Biotechnologies Virtual Enterprise[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 1. Purpose[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis standard defines how the Lazarus Biotechnologies virtual[m
[32m+[m[32menterprise project is documented.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDocumentation is treated as a project deliverable rather than an[m
[32m+[m[32mafterthought.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe objective is to maintain a reproducible historical record of the[m
[32m+[m[32menvironment's design, implementation, testing, security posture,[m
[32m+[m[32mincidents, failures, remediation, and evolution.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 2. Documentation Principles[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mProject documentation should answer, where applicable:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. What was being implemented?[m
[32m+[m[32m2. Why was it necessary?[m
[32m+[m[32m3. What technology or approach was selected?[m
[32m+[m[32m4. What alternatives were considered?[m
[32m+[m[32m5. How was it implemented?[m
[32m+[m[32m6. How was it tested?[m
[32m+[m[32m7. How was successful implementation verified?[m
[32m+[m[32m8. What problems occurred?[m
[32m+[m[32m9. How were those problems resolved?[m
[32m+[m[32m10. What was learned?[m
[32m+[m[32m11. What should happen next?[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mImportant failures and troubleshooting steps should not be removed[m
[32m+[m[32mfrom project history.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 3. Implementation Workflow[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSubstantial project changes should follow:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mLEARN → BUILD → TEST → VERIFY → DOCUMENT → COMMIT[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### LEARN[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mUnderstand the relevant technology, security concept, business[m
[32m+[m[32mrequirement, or control before implementation.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### BUILD[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mImplement the planned change using documented and reproducible steps.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### TEST[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDeliberately test the implementation.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### VERIFY[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mCollect evidence demonstrating that the expected result occurred.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### DOCUMENT[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mRecord configuration, evidence, decisions, problems, and lessons.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### COMMIT[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mCommit the completed and reviewed change to version control.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 4. Implementation Record[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mMajor implementations should record:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Objective[m
[32m+[m[32m- Business requirement[m
[32m+[m[32m- Security requirement[m
[32m+[m[32m- Prerequisites[m
[32m+[m[32m- Architecture[m
[32m+[m[32m- Implementation steps[m
[32m+[m[32m- Configuration[m
[32m+[m[32m- Testing procedure[m
[32m+[m[32m- Verification evidence[m
[32m+[m[32m- Problems encountered[m
[32m+[m[32m- Resolution[m
[32m+[m[32m- Lessons learned[m
[32m+[m[32m- Security considerations[m
[32m+[m[32m- Cost impact[m
[32m+[m[32m- Next steps[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 5. Architecture Decisions[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSignificant architecture decisions must be recorded using an[m
[32m+[m[32mArchitecture Decision Record (ADR).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mADRs should include:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Decision ID[m
[32m+[m[32m- Title[m
[32m+[m[32m- Status[m
[32m+[m[32m- Context[m
[32m+[m[32m- Decision[m
[32m+[m[32m- Alternatives considered[m
[32m+[m[32m- Rationale[m
[32m+[m[32m- Security implications[m
[32m+[m[32m- Cost implications[m
[32m+[m[32m- Consequences[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAccepted ADRs should not be silently rewritten when architecture[m
[32m+[m[32mchanges.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mA new ADR should supersede the previous decision where appropriate.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 6. Evidence[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEvidence may include:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Screenshots[m
[32m+[m[32m- Command output[m
[32m+[m[32m- Configuration files[m
[32m+[m[32m- Queries[m
[32m+[m[32m- Logs[m
[32m+[m[32m- Diagrams[m
[32m+[m[32m- Test results[m
[32m+[m[32m- Dashboard exports[m
[32m+[m[32m- Code[m
[32m+[m[32m- Detection rules[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEvidence should demonstrate a technical or analytical result rather[m
[32m+[m[32mthan exist only for decoration.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSensitive information must be sanitized before publication.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 7. Troubleshooting[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mMeaningful implementation failures should be documented.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mTroubleshooting records should capture:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Observed behavior[m
[32m+[m[32m- Expected behavior[m
[32m+[m[32m- Initial hypothesis[m
[32m+[m[32m- Investigation[m
[32m+[m[32m- Root cause[m
[32m+[m[32m- Resolution[m
[32m+[m[32m- Verification[m
[32m+[m[32m- Lesson learned[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFailures should not be removed merely to make the project appear[m
[32m+[m[32mperfect.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 8. Security Incidents[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSecurity incidents will use separate incident case records.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIncident records should eventually include:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Incident ID[m
[32m+[m[32m- Detection source[m
[32m+[m[32m- Initial alert[m
[32m+[m[32m- Analyst observations[m
[32m+[m[32m- Investigation timeline[m
[32m+[m[32m- Evidence[m
[32m+[m[32m- Scope[m
[32m+[m[32m- Root cause[m
[32m+[m[32m- Containment[m
[32m+[m[32m- Eradication[m
[32m+[m[32m- Recovery[m
[32m+[m[32m- Business impact[m
[32m+[m[32m- Control failures[m
[32m+[m[32m- Recommendations[m
[32m+[m[32m- Lessons learned[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mScenario ground truth must remain separate from analyst-facing[m
[32m+[m[32mevidence until the investigation is complete.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 9. Cost Tracking[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mCloud or paid resources must record:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Resource[m
[32m+[m[32m- Purpose[m
[32m+[m[32m- Provider[m
[32m+[m[32m- Date created[m
[32m+[m[32m- Expected cost[m
[32m+[m[32m- Actual cost[m
[32m+[m[32m- Free-tier applicability[m
[32m+[m[32m- Shutdown procedure[m
[32m+[m[32m- Date removed[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe project's target recurring operating cost is $0 per month.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe soft recurring-cost ceiling is $10 per month unless a higher[m
[32m+[m[32mexpense is explicitly justified.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 10. Versioning[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mImportant datasets and architecture states must be versioned.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mHistorical state should not be overwritten when preserving it[m
[32m+[m[32mprovides analytical or portfolio value.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mExamples include:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Workforce snapshots[m
[32m+[m[32m- Architecture versions[m
[32m+[m[32m- Security maturity[m
[32m+[m[32m- Asset inventory[m
[32m+[m[32m- Access assignments[m
[32m+[m[32m- Risk register[m
[32m+[m[32m- Control implementation[m
[32m+[m[32m- Project metrics[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 11. Publication[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe public repository and portfolio must never intentionally contain:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Real credentials[m
[32m+[m[32m- API tokens[m
[32m+[m[32m- Private keys[m
[32m+[m[32m- Personal sensitive information[m
[32m+[m[32m- Actual CUI[m
[32m+[m[32m- Classified information[m
[32m+[m[32m- Real patient information[m
[32m+[m[32m- Customer data[m
[32m+[m[32m- Hidden scenario ground truth[m
[32m+[m[32m- Unsafe attack infrastructure details[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAll company information is synthetic unless explicitly documented[m
[32m+[m[32motherwise.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 12. Definition of Done[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mA major project task is not complete merely because the technology[m
[32m+[m[32mworks.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mA task is complete when:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Implementation is complete[m
[32m+[m[32m- Testing is complete[m
[32m+[m[32m- Verification evidence exists[m
[32m+[m[32m- Documentation is updated[m
[32m+[m[32m- Sensitive information has been reviewed[m
[32m+[m[32m- Changes are committed to version control[m
